  "title": "The Backpack Swap",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "cooperation",
  "premise": "Two hikers in a toy landscape cannot reach a lookout because one has a wide pack that catches on narrow arches and the other has a tall pack that hits low beams. They exchange packs at the route junction, each takes the fitting path, and meet at the overlook with the other’s picnic.",
  "hook": "We brought the right bags to the wrong paths.",
  "visible_action": "Wide pack wedges at an arch; tall pack taps a beam; packs switch; split paths converge at a picnic spot.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Reassigning resources can be better than forcing a fit.",
  "gate": "Use toy terrain with no real climbing or packing safety advice.",
